      "final_text": "Finding acknowledged (`b684115a5b7a`).\n\n**Vulnerability:** Cross-account object read (CWE-639) on `target`.\n\n- `/protected/{account}` correctly enforces ownership (`token-a-public` \u2192 `/protected/B` = 403 denied).\n- `/objects/{account}` authenticates the bearer token but never checks ownership, so `GET /objects/B` with `Authorization: Bearer token-a-public` returns `200 {\"object\":\"private-B\"}`.\n- Controls: no auth \u2192 400; token B on `/objects/B` \u2192 200; token A on `/objects/A` \u2192 200.\n\nNo HTTP transaction digests were available (`list_http_transactions` returned 0), so the finding was filed with the PoC and evidence instead.",
